Subject: [PATCH 70/70] fix: missing server mesanims (scared, sleep) that throw
 mid-dialogue
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. Talk-to on the Lumbridge Doomsayer throws `IllegalStateException: Error Loading MesAnim` from
`Dialogue.mesanim` (via `LumbridgeAdvisors.getScared`): `mesanim.scared` is in `mesanim.rscm` (13) but has no entry
in the server's `mesanim.toml`, so `ServerCacheManager.getMesAnim` returns null. The exception escapes the player's
cycle and the player is disconnected. Port Sarim's sleeping guard uses `mesanim.sleep`, which exists in neither file
and fails the same way.

Change. `mesanim.toml` gains `mesanim.scared` with the `chatscared1-4` sequences (the ones `mesanim.worried`
already uses). The guard uses `bored` instead of the nonexistent `sleep`. New `MesAnimTypesTest` checks that every
mesanim name used in content resolves.

Tests. `MesAnimTypesTest` (`:content:quest:test`) fails before the change (missing `mesanim.scared`) and passes
after. Manual: the Doomsayer's dialogue plays to the end on the RuneLite desktop client.

Data. `chatscared1-4` for `scared` mirror `worried` (both are the scared chat-head set in the cache; which one OSRS
uses for each name is not documented). There is no sleep chat-head animation in the cache; `bored` is a choice.
Needs patch 12 (QuestTalkFixture) for the test.

